  "title": "Ibm Security Advisories - 2026-09-03",
  "description": "Merged 7 ibm security advisories published on 2026-09-03. Original advisory IDs: IBM-7285133, IBM-7286213, IBM-7286233, IBM-7286220, IBM-7286279, IBM-7286274, IBM-7286283\n\nTitles:\n- Multiple security vulnerabilities are addressed with IBM Content Cortex(CCx) 26.0.0-IF002 for August 2026\n- IBM Maximo Application Suite - Predict Component uses multiple dependencies which are vulnerable to multiple CVEs.\n- Multiple vulnerabilities in IBM MQ Operator and Queue manager container images\n- Due to the use of mchange-commons-java, IBM webMethods BPM is vulnerable to Unsafe Reflection ( CVE-2026-55153 )\n- MongoDB Enterprised Advanced affected by: Improper Authorization (CVE-2026-33186)\n- MongoDB Enterprised Advanced affected by: Deserialization of Untrusted Data (CVE-2026-41409, CVE-2026-41635)\n- MongoDB Enterprised Advanced affected by: Deserialization of Untrusted Data (CVE-2026-42778, CVE-2026-42779)",
